# AMD LibM for Windows — our delta from pristine upstream.
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/amd/win-libm  commit 6121d02aef0c775947d5dc655d7fc4ccfe2144ab
#           ("First github commit of AMD LibM for Windows", 2019-07-24)
#           archive sha256 ca15d1bab53cf576ba0bba8c07aa6deac8d2a0fe9d6f219dc35c0d78c5a8d45f
# Apply from sdk/lib/crt/math/libm_sse2/ with: patch -p1 < vendor-patches/amd-libm.patch
#
# THE RECORDED COMMIT IS NOW CONFIRMED. vendor.yaml carried `git commit 6121d02` copied
# out of "3rd Party Files.txt" with an explicit note that it had never been checked
# against github.com/amd/win-libm. It checks out: the commit exists, and against that
# exact tree 17 of our files are byte-identical and the 35 that differ do so by 2-58
# lines each. A wrong base would not look like that.
#
# THE DELTA IS ONE FIX, APPLIED EVERYWHERE: LP64 -> LLP64. AMD wrote this for a world
# where `long` is 64 bits. On Windows x64 `long` is 32 bits, so every place the code
# stuffs a double's bit pattern into a `long`/`unsigned long` truncates. Ours says
# `long long`/`unsigned long long` instead. That is ~240 of the ~257 changed lines,
# including the GET_BITS_DP64/PUT_BITS_DP64 call sites and casts like
# `(double)(long)(dx / w)` in remainder.c. It is a genuine correctness fix, not a style
# change, and it cannot be a -D — it is a type spelled in hundreds of places.
#
# The remainder:
#   ~20 lines   `#pragma function(acos)` and friends wrapped in `#ifdef _MSC_VER`,
#               because clang does not implement that pragma.
#   fma3_available.c  rewritten CRT-startup glue: uses _CRTALLOC/__declspec(allocate)
#               and <intrin.h> rather than <windows.h>/<cruntime.h>/<internal.h>.
#
# NOT IN THIS PATCH — files with no upstream counterpart, i.e. genuinely added here:
#   ELEVEN .asm FILES WERE RE-IMPLEMENTED IN C. Upstream ships L2_by_pi_bits.asm,
#   Lsincos_array.asm, Lsincosf_array.asm, log{,10}_{128,256}_lead_tail_table.asm,
#   log_F_inv_{dword,qword}_table.asm and two_to_jby64{,_head_tail}_table.asm — all MASM
#   constant tables. We carry .c equivalents instead. Re-vendoring means redoing that
#   conversion, so budget for it.
#   Also added: _handle_error.c, ldexp.c, ldexpf.c.
#
# NOTE THERE IS NOT ONE __REACTOS__ MARKER IN THIS ENTIRE TREE. Unlike FreeType, where
# every hunk is guarded and you can get upstream behaviour back by undefining a macro,
# this is an unconditional fork of the sources. Nothing here tells a reader which lines
# are ours; that is what this patch is for.
#
